+## 2. GO Evaluation
+
+### 2.1 GO Strengths
+
+| Attribute | Rating | Notes |
+|-----------|--------|-------|
+| Performance | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Good (faster than Python, slower than Rust) |
+| Concurrency | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Goroutines, channels (excellent) |
+| Simplicity | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Minimal syntax, fast compilation |
+| Deployment | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Single binary, no runtime |
+| Web Services | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Excellent HTTP/net/http |
+| Memory Safety | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ | GC (safer than C, less safe than Rust) |
+| SIMD Support | ⭐⭐ | Limited (via intrinsics, not ergonomic) |
+| FFI | ⭐⭐⭐ | CGo exists, but tricky |
+
+### 2.2 GO Weaknesses (For Our Use Case)
+
+| Weakness | Impact | Why It Matters |
+|----------|--------|----------------|
+| **No AVX-512 intrinsics** | CRITICAL | Cannot optimize Smith tests like Rust |
+| **Garbage Collection** | HIGH | GC pauses incompatible with <1ms latency |
+| **No PyO3 equivalent** | HIGH | Cannot integrate with Python as well as Rust |
+| **No generics until 1.18** | MEDIUM | Less type-safe than Rust for 12-parameter system |
+| **No PyPI ecosystem** | MEDIUM | Cannot leverage Python LLM libraries |
+| **Redundant with Rust** | HIGH | Does same things as Rust, but slower |
+
+### 2.3 Where GO Would Fit (If Used)
+
+**Potential Use Cases:**
+- Backend microservices (HTTP APIs)
+- Concurrent data processing pipelines
+- CLI tools (single binary)
+- SurrealDB client (if Rust client immature)
+
+**But We Already Have:**
+- ✅ Rust for backend (faster, better SIMD, PyO3)
+- ✅ Python for orchestration (better LLM integration)
+- ✅ Rust SurrealDB client exists (or use Python driver)
+
+### 2.4 Decision: ❌ NO GO
+
+**Rationale:**
+
+1. **No Unique Advantage:** Everything GO can do, Rust does better (performance, safety, SIMD)
+2. **Redundancy:** Adding GO would duplicate Rust's role without clear benefit
+3. **Integration Complexity:** PyO3 (Rust→Python) is better than CGo (GO→Python)
+4. **Team Focus:** Better to master Rust + Python + TypeScript than add 4th language
+5. **AVX-512 Critical:** GO's limited SIMD is a deal-breaker for physics optimization
+
+**Exception:** If we need a specific GO library with no Rust/Python equivalent, reconsider for that component only.
