+### Why AVX-512 Matters
+
+**AMD Ryzen AI MAX+:**
+- VLEN = 8 (8x f64 per instruction)
+- VLIW packing: Multiple operations per cycle
+- Zero-copy shared memory
+
+**Python Limitation:**
+- NumPy uses BLAS (not SIMD-optimized for this specific operation)
+- GIL prevents true parallelism
+- Memory copying overhead
+
+**Rust Advantage:**
+```rust
+// Rust with AVX-512 intrinsics
+use std::arch::x86_64::*;
+
+#[inline(always)]
+fn dot_product_avx512(a: &[f64], b: &[f64]) -> f64 {
+    unsafe {
+        let mut sum = _mm512_setzero_pd();
+        
+        // Process 8 doubles at once
+        for i in (0..a.len()).step_by(8) {
+            let va = _mm512_loadu_pd(&a[i]);
+            let vb = _mm512_loadu_pd(&b[i]);
+            let prod = _mm512_mul_pd(va, vb);
+            sum = _mm512_add_pd(sum, prod);
+        }
+        
+        // Horizontal sum
+        let result = _mm512_reduce_add_pd(sum);
+        result
+    }
+}
+
+// This is 8x faster than Python loop!
+```
