+#### Requirement 1.3: AVX-512 Optimization
+
+**User Story:** As a performance engineer, I want AVX-512 intrinsics for dot products, so that we achieve 8x parallelism on AMD Ryzen AI MAX+.
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+```rust
+use std::arch::x86_64::*;
+
+#[target_feature(enable = "avx512f")]
+unsafe fn dot_product_8x_parallel(a: &[f64], b: &[f64]) -> f64 {
+    // Process 8 doubles per instruction
+    let mut sum = _mm512_setzero_pd();
+    for i in (0..a.len()).step_by(8) {
+        let va = _mm512_loadu_pd(&a[i]);
+        let vb = _mm512_loadu_pd(&b[i]);
+        let prod = _mm512_mul_pd(va, vb);
+        sum = _mm512_add_pd(sum, prod);
+    }
+    _mm512_reduce_add_pd(sum)
+}
+
+// Performance: 8x faster than scalar implementation
+```
+
+**✓ Benchmark:** 1000 dot products in <1ms
+**✓ Correctness:** Results match scalar version within ±0.0001
+**✓ Fallback:** Non-AVX-512 CPUs use scalar version
